522] assume that we are given a set of initial entities for each query."},{"id":"c3","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_6450d43634bcc2d0","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":2,"quote":"Given a new query, HippoRAG identifies the key concepts in the query and runs the Personalized PageRank (PPR) algorithm [30] on the KG, using the query concepts as the seeds, to integrate information across passages for retrieval."},{"id":"c4","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_fab306facd5b5f68","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":2,"quote":"In this case, it gathers relevant news articles related to the user’s query."},{"id":"c5","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_0d1bed6e900c722e","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":17,"quote":"For TriviaQA, we ﬁlter out answer candidates if they do not occur in top 1000 documents for the query."},{"id":"c6","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_8d4259233c3f5e2a","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":8,"quote":"Query Rewrite.The original queries are not always optimal for LLM retrieval,"},{"id":"c7","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_c7c4761d7fb96ad6","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":5,"quote":"For a given positive text-relation pair (t+, r+), we employ an instruction template on t+ to generate a new text t+ inst = “Instruct: retrieve relations that are present in the given text \\n Query: {t+}”."},{"id":"c8","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_89b5480fb8b7df43","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":27,"quote":"Besides, the model does not accurately capture the beginning and ending years of the war, which are essential for the query."},{"id":"c9","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_3e66e086bac3b1f0","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":25,"quote":"This occurs when multiple passages exist in the corpus that discuss very similar topics since the PPR algorithm is not able to leverage query context directly."},{"id":"c10","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_bfbda37929aab298","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":16,"quote":"For structured knowledge, the CoK method [106] first extracts facts pertinent to the input query from a knowledge graph, then integrates these facts as hints within the input, enhancing performance in knowledge graph question-answering"},{"id":"c11","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_eaeadf987e64c603","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":8,"quote":"1) Query Expansion: Expanding a single query into mul- tiple queries enriches the content of the query, providing further context to address any lack of specific nuances, thereby ensuring the optimal relevance of the generated answers."},{"id":"c12","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_b6d1346de8bafc2d","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":8,"quote":"“Who is the President of Peru?”) to query our NQ RAG model with each index."},{"id":"c13","chunkId":"743155d9b0541c99_c_43f9b3c00e35000e","docId":"743155d9b0541c99","docTitle":"2401.15391_MultiHop_RAG_Benchmarking_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Multi_Hop","page":1,"quote":"n necessi- tates retrieving and reasoning over evidence from multiple documents, a process known as multi-hop query."},{"id":"c14","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_682f79d20bd7bb96","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":3,"quote":"), q(x) = BERTq(x) where d(z) is a dense representation of a document produced by a BERTBASE document encoder [8], and q(x) a query representation produced by a query encoder, also based on BERTBASE."},{"id":"c15","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_b5d8e0c839c60e39","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":22,"quote":"In this case, the name of the query named entity, “Alhandra”, is equivalent to its KG node."},{"id":"c16","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_18d9f568d1c19f4e","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":10,"quote":"(Middle) Recursive retrieval involves gradually refining the user query and breaking down the problem into sub-problems, then continuously solving complex problems through retrieval and generation."},{"id":"c17","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_f2896d5f55e04d17","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":4,"quote":"Routing in the RAG system navigates through diverse data sources, selecting the optimal pathway for a query, whether it involves summarization, specific database searches, or merging different information streams [19]."},{"id":"c18","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_f3bfbf66a31a30d7","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":9,"quote":"In this approach, the retriever module is directly substituted to gen- erate relevant documents according to a query."},{"id":"c19","chunkId":"730f1a9f38d16689_c_5f423bf2ac5ccfdd","docId":"730f1a9f38d16689","docTitle":"2404.16130_From_Local_to_Global_A_Graph_RAG_Approach_to_Query_Focused_Summarizati","page":5,"quote":"These summaries are independently useful as a way to understand the global structure and semantics of the dataset, and may themselves be used to make sense of a corpus in the absence of a specific query."},{"id":"c20","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_ff1814eb2a0b5efa","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":4,"quote":"Common methods include query rewriting query transformation, query expansion and other techniques [7], [9]–[11]."},{"id":"c21","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_9575a1b71371de3e","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":3,"quote":"We do not ﬁnd this step necessary for strong performance, and keep the document encoder (and index) ﬁxed, only ﬁne-tuning the query encoder BERTq and the BART generator."},{"id":"c22","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_2428bbb77a4838ab","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":29,"quote":"{\"named_entities\": [\"First for Women\", \"Arthur’s Magazine\"]} Input: Question: QUERY TO INDEX Query NER (Retrieval) Figure 8: Prompt for query NER during retrieval."},{"id":"c23","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_ae8def7c1ab8790b","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":2,"quote":"(a) Query generation relies on the log probability of LLMs to gen- erate the query based on the passage."},{"id":"c24","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_e986e8309a32186a","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":4,"quote":"It concate- nates the query and passage with a [SEP] token and estimates relevance using the representation of the [CLS] token."},{"id":"c25","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_3fa0659d7f419fcb","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":3,"quote":"It then computes the similarity scores between the query vector and the vector of chunks within the indexed corpus."},{"id":"c26","chunkId":"743155d9b0541c99_c_f02eb32a3c5fe618","docId":"743155d9b0541c99","docTitle":"2401.15391_MultiHop_RAG_Benchmarking_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Multi_Hop","page":4,"quote":"Below, we explain the specifications for different multi-hop query types."},{"id":"c27","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_b66d789a66166909","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":19,"quote":"In a similar vein, RoK [431] first uses chain of thoughts reasoning to expand the original query, extracting the seed entities from the expanded query."},{"id":"c28","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_38470e14d01b3cab","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":7,"quote":"For example, the information that connects the knowledge graph and the query \"Who is Justin Bieber’s brother?\" is not a specific passage but instead the entity \"Justin Bieber\" and the relation \"brother of\"."},{"id":"c29","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_b29b11771becd699","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":19,"quote":"Consequently, the average running time per query is 11 seconds for gpt-3.5-turbo and 32 seconds for gpt-4."},{"id":"c30","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_9599874139ef14c4","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":9,"quote":"In addition to using LLM for query rewriting, specialized smaller language models, such as RRR (Rewrite-retrieve-read) [7]."},{"id":"c31","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_c40cdf434f10fa6a","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":12,"quote":"The search query is: {{query}} I will rank the {{num}} passages above based on their relevance to the search query."},{"id":"c32","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_8b2e6c5acfee6f6a","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":2,"quote":"For query x, we use Maximum Inner Product Search (MIPS) to ﬁnd the top-K documents zi."},{"id":"c33","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_3fa0659d7f419fcb","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":3,"quote":"Upon receipt of a user query, the RAG system employs the same encoding model utilized during the indexing phase to transform the query into a vector representation."},{"id":"c34","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_8ee179fd01b95821","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":8,"quote":"2.3.4 Query Decomposition Query decomposition [447] aims to split the input query into multiple distinct subqueries, which are used to first retrieve sub-results and aggregate these sub-results together for the final results."},{"id":"c35","chunkId":"ac529ab762fd1672_c_63366a50187da7c6","docId":"ac529ab762fd1672","docTitle":"HybridRAG: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Vector Retrieval Augmented Generation for Efficient Information Extraction","page":2,"quote":"Then, the generative model takes this retrieved context along with the original query and synthesizes a response."},{"id":"c36","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_e2cb235211566f42","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":19,"quote":"In terms of average USD cost, GPT-4 is the most expensive, with a cost of $0.596 per query."},{"id":"c37","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_8dabb5c009f11200","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":4,"quote":"More formall